d that they included a thermal system  to keep the phone cooler now that is  true and the 14 pro Max does do a better  job at it but it does still dim now with  the 14 pro which I'll also talk about in  just a bit with another issue this thing  actually dims even more so than the  regular 14. uh when I when we're doing  our tests when we're doing gaming I'm  honestly really surprised by how much it  dims because of that powerful a16  processor the cooling system is  overwhelmed so that would recommend if  you're on the fence to go for a 14 pro  now the third one is the magsafe  charging speed now I'm somebody that  loves wireless charging I don't even  have like the cable in my room to charge  up but in times where I do need a charge  and we'll talk about battery life in a  bit when I pop it on the speed just  isn't that great now when Apple launched  it we were so excited because we were  finally going to get fast wireless  charging on the iPhone but in my insane  charging comparison I found that their  15 watt magsafe actually wasn't that  much faster than using a 7.5 watt  standard charger because it slows down  to 6 Watts not long after you start  charging so even though C seems like  it's a lot faster it's not and that's  just because Apple slows it in town  which brings me to this video sponsor  ESR which makes my favorite budget three  in one charger their Halo lock wireless  charger with cryo boost now the price is  unbelievably low for the quality and not  only does the airpods charger have  magnetic alignment but since you used  your own Apple watch Puck you'll get  faster charging than budget built-in  options their cryobboost Tech has a fan  so your wireless charging won't slow  down due to heat say if you're watching  videos or doing anything else and having  active cooling increases battery  longevity because unlike other wireless  chargers your phone stays really really  cool and I was shocked by how nice the  thing is especially with the real  aluminum parts the adjustable angles and  the included power adapter whereas other  budget options are plastic and often  don't come with a power brick esr's  magnets are stronger and the fan is  quiet but can also be shut off along  with the lights Apple's Puck can only  charge one device and belkins which has  three costs 150 dollars so I think it's  the best three month charger for the  price check it out using the links below  now like I said I love macsafe and if  you're charging at night it doesn't  matter and with that you can just get  like an ESR one if you're not going to  be waiting for it to charge but I would  love them to maintain that faster speed  when you do need it to charge fast like  for example you have OnePlus that can  charge your phone in 45 minutes when you  need it but then at night it will charge  slower because you don't and it doesn't  want to add the extra heat now with that  we have reverse wireless charging now  this phone is capable of it but Apple  won't let us use it now I know that most  of the time it is not something that's  needed but hear me out on this the  hardware has been in the iPhone since  the iPhone 11 but was never turned on  and the first and only accessory that  can use it is the maxafe battery pack  that came out not long ago now if you  have the battery pack on your phone but  you plug your lightning cable into the  phone itself not the pack well that'll  actually charge your phone faster and  then it will reverse wirelessly charge  the pack so you have the benefit of  having it there and both will charge up  but other than that you can't use that  feature anywhere else now in the last  two months I've had multiple situations  where it would be so nice to have that  once my airpods were dead and I didn't  have access to a charger so I was out of  luck and I was doing a bunch of stuff  outside without using my airpods now I  would have loved it if I could just  place them on my iPhone and charge them  now if you say that's because it is  inefficient well with Apple's battery  pack that first limited to 5 Watts but  then nine months later they upped it  because people weren't happy and it was  slow and you rather have the extra speed  even if we had a 50 inefficiency in my  14 pro Max would lose 25 battery if you  fully charge the airpods in the case but  in case of an emergency in about five  minutes or so you can get an hour of  listening and that's enough to get you  out of a bind and with that they already  added macsafe alignment to the case of  the airpods now other times we're to  revive friends or my wife's dead phone  if they needed to make a call or check  messages and be so nice to be able to  you know plug it up charge charge up a  few percentages and check it or be able  to charge other accessories like an  Apple Watch since they have small enough  batteries where you don't have to drain  your phone that much I just wish that  Apple didn't lock down all the great  Hardware with their software now the  next one has been the lack of the Sim  slot now I wish Apple just kept it here  in the states just like they did in  other countries at first I had issues  with calls not coming in and errors but  after that it stopped now what I'm  having is just the lack of ability to  quickly pull out a Sim put it into  another phone that I'm testing or put it  into a tablet you have to transfer it it  takes a lot longer you just don't want  to do it and with the 14 plus I had to  go in and make multiple calls and then  go into a local spot go through multiple  people to try to get it set up because  of other issues so if they would have  just kept it there like they did in  other countries that would just been a  lot easier for me having no sim slot has  been all negatives with no positives at  all now the next one is the dynamic  Island now I actually absolutely love  the dynamic Island I love that it's very  convenient but we were here two months  later and not many companies already  adding anything to make it useful and I  want them to do that uh so the island is  there itself and the negative is the  fact that it cuts into video uh it you  know it's more noticeable compared to  the notch but I would love it if Google  Maps would allow it to show turn-by-turn  navigation there just like Apple Maps  has and so recently I've actually been  using Apple Maps uh because it is  convenient when I have just set up on my  stand now as you know I have done a ton  of testing with the cameras with every  scenario that you can even against a pro  camera setup that was around nine  thousand dollars and the raw looks  amazing that we have such a huge  difference between shooting regular  photos and the 48 megapixel Pro raw not  only in detail but the ability to have  much better highlight roll off it looks  a lot more natural now I've complained a  lot that you can't shoot 48 megapixel  compressed files and that the file sizes  instead of being three megabytes or  maybe up to seven it's like 75 megabytes  and apple won't let you just shoot to  that now my workaround has been to use  the shortcut to be able to select them  and convert them that's been the best  way that I've found so now I'm shooting  you know a ton of shots doing Pro raw  because it looks so good now other than  just letting us shoot it without having  the conversions I would love to be able  to do portraits in full quality now  Apple doesn't like to have uh features  that take a lot of time like processing  later or that won't be able to show you  the portrait ahead of time but a lot of  Androids do that and I think most of us  would take the trade off of having to  see the image later but get the best  quality now with that I also found that  these new Pro iPhones are doing things a  little bit differently when I did the  comparison against the 13 Pro and 12 Pro  there are some times where the images  didn't look better at all and sometimes  when they actually looked worse and not  just with the main camera and what I  found is the fact that they actually  will not go into night mode they'll just  take a regular photo and that's even  without having the prefer a faster  shutter option turned on now that just  means that you're not getting the better  quality uh because you just press and  take one image now once again for  Android sometimes you take five seconds  or seven seconds when it did the  comparison against the Samsung and the  pixel and that helps them so what I  found is a workaround is the ability to  just go down press that little button  for a night mode drag the slider and  then manually enable night mode but  thing is it just doesn't stick so if you  want the best quality images you have to  do that and there's no way to kind of  enable it to prefer night mode in the  settings and after talking about all  these photos I have to talk about the  lightning Port now I recently made a  video saying I don't want USBC on the  iPhone I want something better and  that's because Apple at this point is  purely I don't know if it's just greed  for money or what but they're limiting  this to be 10 times slower than what we  had in the 12.9 inch iPad in 2015 even  though we actually have the need for it  with large you know raw files we have  prores to back stuff up they're just  capping it and they don't have to be  doing that to me it just doesn't make  sense in you know the end of 2022 almost  2023. now if they do stick with the USB  type-c port I really hope that they're  going to do Thunderbolt like we had a  recenter leak that will fix all of those  issues but Apple just intentionally  wants to keep you using iCloud and  paying for that or at least using  airdrop which they had in their document  so they showed off so that you have to  have a Mac and you're preferring you  know to stay in their ecosystem now the  next one is the fact that the screen is  still too bright often times in the dark  now we talked about the Dual sensors and  people said that it would adjust over  time but it is still brighter in almost  every scenario than before now all Apple  has to do is give you a compensation  adjustment slider in the settings if you  prefer a brighter or darker and that  will also help with battery life I  complained about battery life being  really bad so much so that I had to go  with the 14 pro Max instead of my  preferred smaller size because the  regular 14 pro would die hours earlier  compared to the last generation now  thankfully it has gotten a lot better  and with iOS 16.1 there's been a nice  jump on YouTube idevice help compared  the last four generation of phones and  the 14 pro Max gained just over one and  a half hours of battery life with just  the software update and optimizations so  what's there to complain about well  there's not that much it's definitely a  great thing but that test did not  account for the display being brighter  or the xdr that can get super bright  outside or they're always on display  mode so overall we're still looking at  about one to two hour lower battery life  compared to last year and that's  something that I would gladly take for  these extra features but with that even  though I would like to have the 14 pro  not the pro Max I still have to go with  the pro Max because I do have a lot of  background tasks that need to be on and  the battery life just will not keep up  with the full day this year like it did  last year so there you guys go those are  my frustrations things I wish Apple  didn't do and what they did do along  with some helpful tips there go ahead  and click that Circle above to subscribe  check out one of those great videos  right over there and we'll see you in  the next one  [Music]  thank you

